cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "Acoustic Disguising: Green's function extraction and hologram synthesis"
abstract: >-
  Julia and Python code accompanying the paper "Acoustic disguising: a
  unified framework for cloaking and holography".
  Generates acoustic Green's functions either from an impulsive point source
  or by extracting them from reverberating data via Multi-Dimensional
  Deconvolution (MDD), and uses them to synthesise acoustic holograms.
type: software
